|~ What is declared under `::bind`, the step that declares a name: its
   constructor and the refusals of a declaration, each told in one
   order: the refusal and its page, which repairs the declaration, its
   facts, its laws. ~|

:bind/construct
  |~~ The step of a declaration from its record, `:name`, `:docs` and
      `:body`, which reads back as itself.
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:bind/PayloadNotSchemaError
  |~~ A `::bind` is a map of `:name`, a keyword, `:docs`, a vector of
      docs, and `:body`, a step, and `:field` names the field that does
      not fit: a tag is no name a declaration binds, and the body is the
      step a quote holds, so the declaration `:inc add 1` is
      `{:name :inc :body (~(add 1) | first)} | tag ::bind`.
      ::link~(::bind | doc)
  ~~|

:bind/PayloadNotSchemaError/refusesDocsThatAreNoDocs
  |~~ Docs that are no vector of docs are refused, `:field` naming them. ~~|
  ::law~(::bind{:name :inc :docs [1]} !| [type /field] | eq [::bind/PayloadNotSchemaError :docs])

:bind/PayloadNotSchemaError/refusesATagForAName
  |~~ A tag is no name a declaration binds. ~~|
  ::law~({:name ::Box :body 1} | tag ::bind
    !| [type /field] | eq [::bind/PayloadNotSchemaError :name])

:bind/PayloadNotSchemaError/buildsTheDeclarationOfABody
  |~~ A keyword and the step a quote holds build the declaration. ~~|
  ::law~({:name :inc :body (~(add 1) | first)} | tag ::bind
    | [/] | tag ::quote | eq ~(:inc add 1))

:bind/ReadBackDiffersError
  |~~ The `::bind` prints as text that reads back as another step, and
      `:printed` is that text: a declaration with neither a body nor a
      page prints as the bare keyword, which reads back as the keyword,
      and a body that is a doc prints where a page of the declaration
      stands, and reads back as its page. A declaration binds a body or
      a page, and a doc bound as the value is the body of a group.
      ::link~(::bind | doc)
  ~~|

:bind/ReadBackDiffersError/refusesABindOfNothing
  |~~ A bind with neither a body nor docs prints as a bare name, which
      reads back as another step.
  ~~|
  ::law~(::bind{:name :inc} !| [type /printed] | eq [::bind/ReadBackDiffersError ":inc"])

:bind/ReadBackDiffersError/refusesABodyThatIsADoc
  |~~ A doc as the body reads back as the page of the declaration. ~~|
  ::law~({:name :k :body (~(|~~ x ~~|) | first)} | tag ::bind
    !| type | eq ::bind/ReadBackDiffersError)

:bind/ReadBackDiffersError/bindsADocInAGroup
  |~~ A doc in a group is the value a declaration binds. ~~|
  ::law~(:k (|~~ x ~~|) | k | content | eq " x ")

:bind/EffectMarkMissingError
  |~~ A word whose body calls a name marked `@` reaches outside the
      language, and its own name carries the mark, so every reader of the
      name sees it: `:name` holds the name declared and `:calls` the
      marked name its code calls. The word is declared under its marked
      name, `:any/@fetchAll ~(@fetch …)`. A part whose selector calls a
      marked name is held to the mark of the name it is a part of, which
      runs it at each call, and `:name` is that name.
      ::link~(::bind | doc)
  ~~|

:bind/EffectMarkMissingError/name
  |~~ The name declared without the mark. ~~|
  ::keyword

:bind/EffectMarkMissingError/calls
  |~~ The marked name its code calls. ~~|
  ::keyword

:bind/EffectMarkMissingError/refusesAnUnmarkedWordThatCallsAMarkedName
  |~~ A word that calls a marked name and carries no mark is refused, naming both. ~~|
  ::law~(1 | (:any/bad ~(@callers) | bad)
    !| [type /name /calls]
    |  eq [::bind/EffectMarkMissingError
            :any/bad :@callers])

:bind/EffectMarkMissingError/refusesAWordWhosePartCallsAMarkedName
  |~~ A part whose selector calls a marked name refuses its unmarked word. ~~|
  ::law~(:any/f ~(1) | :any/f/n ~(/0 | @out)
    !| [type /name /calls] | eq [::bind/EffectMarkMissingError :any/f :@out])

:bind/EffectMarkMissingError/takesAWordUnderItsMarkedName
  |~~ A word declared under its marked name is taken. ~~|
  ::law~(:any/@good ~(@callers) | ::any | manifest | has ::any/@good)

:bind/NounNotDeclaredError
  |~~ A name with a path is declared under the noun its path names
      before its last name, and that noun is declared before it, so
      whether the noun is a kind, which the verbs under it serve, is
      known where they are declared: `:name` holds the name and `:noun`
      the noun no declaration made. The noun is declared first, by its
      page, and the names under it after.
      ::link~(::bind | doc)
  ~~|

:bind/NounNotDeclaredError/name
  |~~ The name declared. ~~|
  ::keyword

:bind/NounNotDeclaredError/noun
  |~~ The noun its path names, which no declaration names. ~~|
  ::tag

:bind/NounNotDeclaredError/refusesANameUnderNoNoun
  |~~ A name under a noun no declaration made is refused, naming the noun. ~~|
  ::law~(:Box/area ~(1) !| [type /noun] | eq [::bind/NounNotDeclaredError ::Box])

:bind/NounNotDeclaredError/takesANameUnderADeclaredNoun
  |~~ A name under a noun declared before it runs on the noun's values. ~~|
  ::law~(:Box |~~ A box. ~~| | :Box/area ~(1) | ::Box{} | area | eq 1)

:bind/NameTakenByVocabularyError
  |~~ A value the reader names takes no word of the vocabulary, the name
      of a verb or of a name under a label, since a step that names the
      word means the subject's; a part of a word takes none either, since
      the body reads the part by its name. `:name` holds the name and
      `:addresses` where the word lives. The value or the part takes
      another name, `:limit 5` where `:count 5` is refused.
      ::link~(::bind | doc)
  ~~|

:bind/NameTakenByVocabularyError/name
  |~~ The name, a word of the vocabulary. ~~|
  ::keyword

:bind/NameTakenByVocabularyError/refusesAValueNamedAsAWord
  |~~ A value named as a word is refused with the addresses of the word. ~~|
  ::law~(:count 5
    !| [type /addresses]
    |  eq [::bind/NameTakenByVocabularyError #[::map/count ::set/count ::string/count ::vec/count]])

:bind/NameTakenByVocabularyError/refusesAPartNamedAsAWord
  |~~ A part of a word named as a word is refused. ~~|
  ::law~(:any/f ~(1) | :any/f/count ~(/0)
    !| [type /name] | eq [::bind/NameTakenByVocabularyError :count])

:bind/NameTakenByVocabularyError/takesANameNoWordHolds
  |~~ A name no word holds names a value. ~~|
  ::law~(:limit 5 | [1 2 3] | take limit | eq [1 2 3])

:bind/NameDeclaredTwiceError
  |~~ A name is declared once in a scope: the steps of a pipeline that
      the pipe or the fail track joins share one env, and a declaration
      of a name one of them declared before is refused where it stands,
      `:name` the name. A group, an element, a modifier and a quote open
      scopes of their own, where a name of the
      scope around them is shadowed, so a second value takes another
      name or a group of its own, `(:k 2 | k)`. An address the root holds
      is declared once at all: a reader extends a noun of the root by a
      name of its own, `:vec/second ~(/1)`, and replaces none of its
      names, and a source of the root that declares a name the root holds
      is refused.
      ::link~(::bind | doc)
  ~~|

:bind/NameDeclaredTwiceError/name
  |~~ The name declared again. ~~|
  ::keyword

:bind/NameDeclaredTwiceError/refusesASecondDeclaration
  |~~ A name declared again in its scope is refused. ~~|
  ::law~(:k 1 | :k 2 !| [type /name] | eq [::bind/NameDeclaredTwiceError :k])

:bind/NameDeclaredTwiceError/letsAGroupDeclareAgain
  |~~ A group declares in a scope of its own, so it may name a name again. ~~|
  ::law~(:k 1 | (:k 2 | k) | eq 2)

:bind/NameDeclaredTwiceError/refusesANameTheRootHolds
  |~~ A reader declares no name the root holds. ~~|
  ::law~(:vec/count ~(0) !| type | eq ::bind/NameDeclaredTwiceError)

:bind/NameDeclaredTwiceError/extendsANounOfTheRoot
  |~~ A reader extends a noun of the root by a name of its own. ~~|
  ::law~(:vec/second ~(/1) | [1 2] | second | eq 2)
